 "$comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later. Expected packets worked out from OpenRGB's C++ (commit d4798c120659ec5ba2e664a9e87bedff8d36f880, Controllers/ThermaltakeRiingController) by a separate reference model that mirrors ThermaltakeRiingController::SendInit/SendRGB/SetChannelLEDs, ThermaltakeRiingQuadController::SendInit/SetChannelLEDs (persistent 193-byte channel buffers) and ThermaltakeRiingTrioController::SendInit/SetChannelLEDs (persistent 65-byte buffers, 19-LED chunks) buffer by buffer (openrgb-work/batch2/thermaltake/gen_fixtures.py in the porting session's scratch space, not part of the repository); plugin.js was never run to make them. Each variant gives the LED count of channels 1-5, colour sets in channel order as [r, g, b], and the I/O of Initialize, frames and Shutdown. ops: write = output report (hid_write, whole buffer, report id 0x00 first), read = hid_read_timeout (len, timeout ms). Frame 'shrink' (Quad, Trio) uses the counts in 'counts_shrink' after frame_b, to show the bytes OpenRGB's persistent buffers keep. Riing Shutdown is Lightloom's choice: OpenRGB's Spectrum hardware effect (mode 0x04, speed Normal 0x02) with black colour data; Quad and Trio: black in Direct.",
